From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:37:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07446/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-PUBLISH-042: fix
 adversarial-review findings in ERNIE-Image shim + generate_diagram

Adversarial review of the paperbanana + ERNIE-Image local diagram-generation
backend (REQ-PUBLISH-042) found and this fixes three real issues:

- ernie_image_server.py: the request-model closure fix's first attempt
  (a bare functools.lru_cache) reintroduced the exact FastAPI bug it was
  meant to fix -- get_type_hints resolves string annotations via the
  function's __globals__, so a class returned from a cached function call
  but never assigned to an actual module global is still invisible to it.
  Fixed by publishing the class into globals() under a lock, with
  lru_cache layered on top purely as a cheap-path optimization for callers
  after the first. Re-verified against all 11 tests (they failed with the
  lru_cache-only version, confirming the regression was real).
- generate_diagram.py: the paperbanana-installed precondition check used a
  bare PATH lookup (shutil.which), which misfires with a misleading
  blocked_paperbanana_not_installed verdict when this project's venv isn't
  on PATH even though paperbanana is genuinely installed there. Now checks
  next to the running interpreter (sys.executable's directory) first.
- ernie_image_server.py: documented that the OpenAI Images API's `quality`
  field is accepted but silently unused (ERNIE-Image has no equivalent
  quality-tiering concept), rather than leaving it undocumented.

